{{cquote|Mohun, Sire John de, of Dunster, banneret, baron 1299… bore at the battle of Falkirk 1298, and at the siege of Caerlaverock 1300, or, a cross engrailed sable… his son Sir John (father of Sir John, 2nd Baron, K.G., and a founder) also bore it, with a label (3) gules…}}
